  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "Let \\(f\\) be a linear function for which \\(f(6) - f(2) = 12.\\) What is \\(f(12) - f(2)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(12\\)",
    "B": "\\(18\\)",
    "C": "\\(24\\)",
    "D": "\\(30\\)",
    "E": "\\(36\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Write \\(f(x)=mx+b\\), where \\(m\\) and \\(b\\) are constants. Subtracting two function values cancels \\(b\\), so we can find the needed difference without determining the whole function. The given condition becomes\n\\[\nf(6)-f(2)=(6m+b)-(2m+b)=4m=12,\n\\]\nso \\(m=3\\). Therefore\n\\[\nf(12)-f(2)=(12m+b)-(2m+b)=10m=30.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(30\\), choice D.",
